WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.641 --> 00:00:04.055
- You can't really call me a
crazy cat lady; I'm obsessive.

00:00:04.055 --> 00:00:06.842
I would rather have 800
cats than another man.

00:00:06.842 --> 00:00:08.719
I don't need a man in my life.

00:00:08.719 --> 00:00:11.094
Been there, done that,
bought the t-shirt, no.

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:12.566
Kitty, kitty, kitty, kitty, kitty, kitty.

00:00:12.566 --> 00:00:14.874
Floyd, come on, Cricket.

00:00:14.874 --> 00:00:16.998
(light upbeat music)

00:00:16.998 --> 00:00:20.683
This is called the Cat House on the Kings.

00:00:20.683 --> 00:00:22.691
It's a 12 acre, no cage, no kill,

00:00:22.691 --> 00:00:25.700
sanctuary, rescue adoption center,

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.896
and we also do a a lot
of spays and newters.

00:00:27.896 --> 00:00:30.329
(cat meowing)
Oh, come here Cricket.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:31.162
Come on.

00:00:32.322 --> 00:00:35.155
We have close to 800 adults

00:00:35.155 --> 00:00:36.736
and 300 kittens

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:39.845
on the property as we speak.

00:00:39.845 --> 00:00:41.518
(kitten meowing)

00:00:41.518 --> 00:00:43.034
(bright upbeat music)

00:00:43.034 --> 00:00:44.835
It wasn't like I planned,
"Hey, I think I'll have

00:00:44.835 --> 00:00:47.773
"a thousand cats, what a novel idea."

00:00:47.773 --> 00:00:49.123
It wasn't like that.

00:00:49.123 --> 00:00:51.082
I thought, well, there's always room for more,

00:00:51.082 --> 00:00:52.928
they're gonna kill this one.

00:00:52.928 --> 00:00:55.095
We have way too many cats.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.470
So this, this was my house.

00:00:59.431 --> 00:01:03.348
You can see that it's an
extremely large house.

00:01:06.282 --> 00:01:07.896
- [Interviewer] So you
had to give up your home

00:01:07.896 --> 00:01:09.054
for these cats?

00:01:09.054 --> 00:01:12.043
- I tried for about 16
years to make it work

00:01:12.043 --> 00:01:15.778
but it wasn't okay having
60 something in my bedroom.

00:01:15.778 --> 00:01:20.551
One night they threw up in my
ear and that was when I moved.

00:01:20.551 --> 00:01:22.998
All 4,200 square feet is theirs,

00:01:22.998 --> 00:01:25.998
that's why we call it the Cat House.

00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:31.128
We have saved over
28,000 cats in 24 years.

00:01:32.965 --> 00:01:36.182
We have a staff now of about 45.

00:01:36.182 --> 00:01:39.676
You have to be very on top of the job

00:01:39.676 --> 00:01:43.507
because you have a lot of cats
that your responsible for.

00:01:43.507 --> 00:01:45.980
No point in rescuing
'em and taking them in

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.489
if you can't take care of them.

00:01:47.489 --> 00:01:49.567
You know this is not normal,

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:50.997
people after a while would say,

00:01:50.997 --> 00:01:52.776
"Well, you know, I think
I've done this enough,

00:01:52.776 --> 00:01:55.591
"I think I'll go have a life
now, I think I'll go travel."

00:01:55.591 --> 00:01:56.674
Nope, not me!

00:01:57.622 --> 00:01:59.728
Daphne, look this way.

00:01:59.728 --> 00:02:00.561
Daph!

00:02:01.536 --> 00:02:03.720
Come on, I want you to be on TV.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.970
(bright upbeat music)

